{"actor":"model","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-217279","model_call":12,"attempt":1,"model":"gpt-5.5","usage":{"input_tokens":6481,"output_tokens":318,"total_tokens":6799,"cached_tokens":5376,"reasoning_tokens":148},"output_characters":763,"decision":{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_03_464593931#11_867475502","relevance":3,"reason":"The document is dedicated to the claim of low military pay and provides direct evidence about Congress, pay boosts, retirement, and medical benefits; although not Marine-specific, it directly addresses the shared military compensation system Marines fall under.","learned":"One answer is that the premise is disputed: basic pay may look low, but total military compensation includes substantial retirement and medical benefits, and pay levels are shaped by Congress."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q1642","reason":"This query produced a directly relevant low-military-pay document; continue for more evidence about budget/Congress/underpaid military compensation."}}}
