{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-217279","model_call":16,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1643"},"record":{"query":{"op":"next","qid":"q1643"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_19_169605145#3_184920062","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1643","rank":2,"snippet":"in 1990 was moved one day to the first to save money in a fiscal year.) Major components There are a few components which most military members receive. Basic pay Also known as \"base pay\", this is given to members of the active duty military on a monthly basis and is determined by their rank (or more appropriately their pay grade) and their length of time in military service. Basic pay is the same for all the services. Title 37 U.S.C. 1009 provides a permanent formula for an automatic annual military pay raise that indexes the raise to the annual increase in the <cover>Employment Cost Index (ECI). The fiscal year 2010 president's budget request for a 2.9% military pay raise </cover>was consistent with this formula. However, Congress, in financial years 2004, 2005, 2006, 2008, and 2009 approved the pay raise as the ECI increase plus 0.5%. The 2007 pay raise was equal to the ECI.\" , \"start_char\": 1971.000000 , \"title\": \"United States military pay - Wikipedia\" , \"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_military_pay\" }"},"time":8},"model_calls":16,"document_judgments":13,"relevance_3":5,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
